 "assistant_text": "The useful stress test is whether revenue gains survived customer responses and arrived within your deadline—not just whether prices or subscriber numbers increased.\n\n1. It is a year later and this decision went badly because ‘Raise prices by 10%’ set ‘Price rise from current price’, but customer losses eroded the added revenue.\nWatch for: Cancellation requests rose after customers received renewal notices.\nMitigate: Test the change with a small renewal cohort before extending it.\n\n2. It is a year later and this decision went badly because ‘Launch starter tier’ set ‘Starter monthly price’, but ‘Starter subscribers’ grew too slowly to deliver the revenue needed within nine months.\nWatch for: Paid starter sign-ups fell short of the launch plan.\nMitigate: Test paid demand before committing to a full launch.\n\nOutside the model: Could existing customers downgrade to the starter tier, replacing higher-value revenue rather than adding new revenue?\n"
